{"graph_chars": "Good morning. I am Professor Elsa Voss. This lecture is Chapter Two of Principles of Macroeconomics, OpenStax, third edition: Choice in a World of Scarcity. Chapter One gave us scarcity. This chapter prices every yes as a no to something else. We cover opportunity cost, the budget constraint, utility, the production possibilities frontier, productive and allocative efficiency, comparative advantage, positive versus normative statements, and Adam Smith's invisible hand. Economists chuckled when the Rolling Stones recorded You Cannot Always Get What You Want, because they had been singing that tune for decades. Lionel Robbins wrote in nineteen thirty-two that the time at our disposal is limited. There are only twenty-four hours in the day. If we choose one thing we must relinquish others. That is opportunity cost: the value of the next best alternative.", "graph_times": [[0.0, 0.0613], [0.0613, 0.1227], [0.1227, 0.184], [0.184, 0.2454], [0.2454, 0.3067], [0.3067, 0.3681], [0.3681, 0.4294], [0.4294, 0.4908], [0.4908, 0.5521], [0.5521, 0.6134], [0.6134, 0.6748], [0.6748, 0.7361], [0.7361, 0.7975], [0.7975, 0.8588], [0.8588, 0.9202], [0.9202, 0.9815], [0.9815, 1.0429], [1.0429, 1.1042], [1.1042, 1.1655], [1.1655, 1.2269], [1.2269, 1.2882], [1.2882, 1.3496], [1.3496, 1.4109], [1.4109, 1.4723], [1.4723, 1.5336], [1.5336, 1.5949], [1.5949, 1.6563], [1.6563, 1.7176], [1.7176, 1.779], [1.779, 1.8403], [1.8403, 1.9017], [1.9017, 1.963], [1.963, 2.0244], [2.0244, 2.0857], [2.0857, 2.147], [2.147, 2.2084], [2.2084, 2.2697], [2.2697, 2.3311], [2.3311, 2.3924], [2.3924, 2.4538], [2.4538, 2.5151], [2.5151, 2.5765], [2.5765, 2.6378], [2.6378, 2.6991], [2.6991, 2.7605], [2.7605, 2.8218], [2.8218, 2.8832], [2.8832, 2.9445], [2.9445, 3.0059], [3.0059, 3.0672], [3.0672, 3.1286], [3.1286, 3.1899], [3.1899, 3.2512], [3.2512, 3.3126], [3.3126, 3.3739], [3.3739, 3.4353], [3.4353, 3.4966], [3.4966, 3.558], [3.558, 3.6193], [3.6193, 3.6806], [3.6806, 3.742], [3.742, 3.8033], 